# Log Checkpoints (full visibility)

Every component MUST write to `cdc_catalog.logs` at each checkpoint below. Use shared `log_write()` (C++) — never skip a checkpoint.

## Run lifecycle (all commands)

| Checkpoint | Level | Message pattern |
|------------|-------|-----------------|
| Run start | `info` | `{command} started` + `batch_id` |
| Run success | `info` | `{command} completed` + summary counts |
| Run partial | `warning` | `{command} completed with errors` + failure count |
| Run fatal | `error` | `{command} failed` + error detail |
| External connect fail | `error` | `{engine} connect failed` |

## Catalog (`component=catalog`)

| Checkpoint | Level |
|------------|-------|
| Per `conn_id` start | `info` |
| MariaDB tables scanned | `info` + `tables_discovered` |
| Upsert + prune done | `info` + `upserted`, `pruned` |
| PK sync done | `info` + `pk_updated` |
| Per `conn_id` done | `info` + all stats |
| Per `conn_id` error | `error` + exception |
| Empty source scan | `warning` |

## MariaDB full load (`component=mariadb_load`)

| Checkpoint | Level |
|------------|-------|
| Run start | `info` + runtime batch/workers from `runtime_config` |
| Full load schema batch | `info` + `table_count`, `parallel_tables` |
| Table start | `info` |
| After TRUNCATE | `info` |
| DDL sync done | `info` + columns/indexes/FKs added |
| Table COPY done | `info` + `rows_loaded`, `duration_ms` |
| Table error | `error` |
| Run end | `info` or `warning` |

**Per-table order:** ensure base table → **TRUNCATE** → **DDL sync** (columns, indexes, FKs) → **COPY** (parents before children via FK sort).

## MariaDB CDC (`component=mariadb_cdc`)

| Checkpoint | Level |
|------------|-------|
| Run start | `info` + max_seconds, max_events |
| Conn start | `info` + binlog file/position, table count |
| Conn skipped (no position) | `warning` |
| Conn completed | `info` + events, upserts, deletes, checkpoint |
| Conn error | `error` |
| Run end | `info` or `warning` |

## Context JSON (always include when relevant)

`duration_ms`, row counts, `sqlstate`, `stop_reason`, `service_tier` — **never credentials**.
